\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Who is on the Lord's side?
\par Who will serve the King?
\par Who will be His helpers
\par Other lives to bring?
\par Who will leave the world's side?
\par Who will face the foe?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who is on the Lord's side?
\par Who for Him will go?
\par By Thy call of mercy,
\par By Thy grace divine,
\par We are on the Lord's side;
\par Saviour we are Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Jesus, Thou has brought us,
\par Not with gold or gem,
\par But with Thine own life-blood,
\par For Thy diadem.
\par With Thy blessing filling
\par Each who comes to Thee,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thou hast made us willing,
\par Thou hast made us free.
\par By Thy great redemption,
\par By Thy grace divine,
\par We are on the Lord's side;
\par Saviour, we are Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fierce may be the conflict,
\par Strong may be the foe;
\par But the King's own army
\par None can overthrow.
\par Round His standard ranging,
\par Victory is secure;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par For His truth unchanging
\par Makes the triumph sure.
\par Joyfully enlisting,
\par By Thy grace divine,
\par We are on the Lord's side;
\par Saviour, we are Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Chosen to be soldiers
\par In an alien land,
\par Chosen, called, and faithful,
\par For our Captain's band,
\par In the service royal
\par Let us not grow cold;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Let us be right loyal,
\par Noble, true, and bold.
\par Master, Thou wilt keep us,
\par By Thy grace divine,
\par Always on the Lord's side,
\par Saviour, always Thine.
\par Amen.
\par 
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

